    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Kostya approaches Viktor's table to try and swap the poisoned cognac bottle back. Viktor gets angry and tells him to go away. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извините, приятного вам вечера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что тебе нужно от меня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мне нужна эта бутылка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "О чём ты говоришь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я возьму эту бутылку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А вам поставлю другую.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тебе что, совсем нечего делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, я просто хочу дать другую.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Не трогай ничего, иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но я должен её забрать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я сказал, иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятно, давай дальше.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извините, приятного вам вечера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excuse me, have a pleasant evening.' Kostya uses the polite plural 'you' here alongside 'sorry', keeping a formal or respectful tone.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что тебе нужно от меня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What do you need from me?' Russian expresses this impersonally, literally saying 'to me' or 'to you' with 'me'. Then Kostya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мне нужна эта бутылка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I need this bottle.' Notice how 'to me' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'bottle'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "О чём ты говоришь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What are you talking about?' Russian forms this yes-or-no question without a question word, relying on rising pitch on 'you say'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я возьму эту бутылку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will take this bottle.' Kostya combines 'I' with 'a bottle' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А вам поставлю другую.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I will put another one for you.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'and' with 'the other one'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тебе что, совсем нечего делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you have absolutely nothing to do?' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'for you' with 'do'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, я просто хочу дать другую.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, I just want to give another one.' Notice how 'no' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'the other one'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Не трогай ничего, иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do not touch anything, get out of here!' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'not' with 'from here'. Then Kostya responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но я должен её забрать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But I must take it.' Kostya links 'but' directly with 'I' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я сказал, иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I said, get out of here!' Chef Viktor combines 'I' with 'from here' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятно, давай дальше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
